{"availability":"available","full":"bhmj/jsonslice","name":"jsonslice","description":"json slicer","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":91,"forks":11,"created":"2018-05-02T00:33:15Z","updated":"2024-10-25T16:43:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":["golang","jsonpath","jsonslice","slice"],"demo":"https://play.golang.org/p/fYv-Y12akvs","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:32.681Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:32.681Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:32.681Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:18.944Z","stars":91,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:32.681Z","stars":91,"forks":11}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["JSON Slice is a Go package which allows to execute fast jsonpath queries without unmarshalling the whole data.","Sometimes you need to get a single value from incoming json using jsonpath, for example to route data accordingly or so. To do that you must unmarshall the whole data into interface{} struct and then apply some jsonpath library to it, only to get just a tiny little value. What a waste of resourses! Well, now there's jsonslice.","Simply call jsonslice.Get on your raw json data to slice out just the part you need. The []byte received can then be unmarshalled into a struct or used as it is."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhmj/jsonslice/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"aa82de905f19d1ebf282cce9d46973710578283b06d2ccae4e2bb9d2cd8875d5","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:27:05.134Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:18.643Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-10-25T16:43:05Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:18.645Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"JSON Slice is a Go package which allows to execute fast jsonpath queries without unmarshalling the whole data.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bhmj/jsonslice/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"aa82de905f19d1ebf282cce9d46